Non-generative decision models assign probabilities to supplied options without writing an answer. System-One Control Bench tests whether these decisions can guide navigation across 100 symbolic gridworld puzzles, ten input conditions and five action spaces. An exact solver identifies every optimal move, including ties. DeepSeek V4.1 Flash (reasoning) has the highest won rate among the models: 80% with full context. Jev wins 57%; paired comparisons do not establish an advantage over Gemma or DeepSeek without reasoning. Supplying simulated outcomes improves Jev's navigation, but larger sets of sequence moves do not consistently help. Laya and GLiClass stay near random with the map alone. On shared exam positions, Jev and Gemma both reach 90% full-context optimality. For Jev, this exceeds its own-game optimality even after matching puzzle weighting: good isolated decisions do not ensure completed games.
